// allowedImports lists the internal packages each internal package may
// import. go test runs in internal/, so "./..." never reaches cmd/neurokit,
// which may import anything.

// The client must not reach into server internals, and runner must not
// depend on the wire format. A new package fails until it has a row, so its
// place is decided on purpose. Test-only imports are not checked.

// Package wire defines what crosses HTTP between the neurokit client and a
// broker, and what a handler writes on fd 3: the error body, the shared codes
// and their HTTP statuses, the write outcome, and strict JSON decoding.

// Every body neurokit reads is meant to go through DecodeOneJSONValue: request
// arguments, handler and broker answers, and the manifest. Two existing
// brokers cap no body size and accept an empty body. A write value such as
// "Sent" must fail here, not pass on as the handler's own outcome.

// JSON decoding rejects a write value that ParseWriteState does not
// accept, such as "Sent" or "done". A JSON null skips this check and
// leaves the value empty, which later counts as unknown.

// In cases where the write status is missing or unknown, or contradicts
// the error code, this function marks the change as unknown. This function
// prevents outputs like "success" + "WriteStateUnknown" and
// "provider-rejected" + "WriteStateUnknown" and replaces them with
// "change-unknown" + "WriteStateUnknown".
